  "question": "1) Background / Context\n\nThe project involves the development of a comprehensive database system for managing data related to California schools. This database includes geospatial information, SAT average scores, and Free or Reduced-Price Meal (FRPM) eligibility data. The system aims to provide an integrated view of various indicators of educational performance and student needs across the state.\n\n2) Objectives\n\nThe main objective is to create a robust data repository that consolidates school performance and demographic information. This will support educational stakeholders in making data-driven decisions to improve educational outcomes and resource allocation.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users\n\n- Stakeholders:\n  - State education authorities\n  - School district administrators\n  - Educational policy analysts\n  - Researchers\n\n- Users:\n  - School administrators\n  - Education researchers \n  - Policy makers\n\n4) Functional Descriptions\n\n- Data Storage:\n  - Maintain detailed records for each school, including unique identifiers, location, and administrative details.\n  - Store SAT score data, including average scores and percentage of students scoring above 1500.\n  - Record data on Free or Reduced-Price Meal eligibility by percentage and count for various age groups.\n  \n- Data Relationships:\n  - Establish relationships between schools and their performance and demographic data through a unique school code (CDSCode).\n  \n- Data Retrieval:\n  - Allow users to query school data using key identifiers such as school name, district name, or school code.\n  \n- Integration:\n  - Ensure the database is capable of updating with new school information, SAT scores, and FRPM data as it becomes available.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Performance:\n  - Support efficient querying and retrieval of data for potentially large datasets.\n  \n- Scalability:\n  - Design the system to accommodate expanding datasets as more schools and updated yearly data are added.\n  \n- Security:\n  - Implement suitable access controls to protect sensitive student and school data.\n  \n- Reliability:\n  - Ensure high availability and reliability of the database, minimizing downtime and data loss risks.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0097\nCREATE TABLE `schools` (\n  `cds_code` varchar(14) NOT NULL,\n  `school_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `district_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `county_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `street_address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `city` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `state` char(2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `zip_code` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `latitude` decimal(10,7) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `longitude` decimal(10,7) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `school_type` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`cds_code`),\n  KEY `schools_school_name_idx` (`school_name`),\n  KEY `schools_district_name_idx` (`district_name`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `sat_scores` (\n  `sat_score_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `cds_code` varchar(14) NOT NULL,\n  `report_year` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `average_ebrw_score` decimal(6,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `average_math_score` decimal(6,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `average_total_score` decimal(6,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `pct_above_1500` decimal(5,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`sat_score_id`),\n  KEY `sat_scores_cds_code_idx` (`cds_code`),\n  KEY `sat_scores_year_idx` (`report_year`),\n  CONSTRAINT `sat_scores_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`cds_code`) REFERENCES `schools` (`cds_code`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `frpm_data` (\n  `frpm_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `cds_code` varchar(14) NOT NULL,\n  `report_year` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `total_enrollment` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `frpm_count` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `frpm_percentage` decimal(5,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `k_12_frpm_count` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `k_12_frpm_percentage` decimal(5,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `age_5_17_frpm_count` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `age_5_17_frpm_percentage` decimal(5,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`frpm_id`),\n  KEY `frpm_data_cds_code_idx` (`cds_code`),\n  KEY `frpm_data_year_idx` (`report_year`),\n  CONSTRAINT `frpm_data_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`cds_code`) REFERENCES `schools` (`cds_code`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
